I am walking slowly in the quiet halls of the museum.
Here it is completely silent and peaceful.
There is a display of ancient things in front of me.
These are old pots and those are some coins.
I look carefully at this big clay pot.
Next to it, there is a small board.
I read the information written on that board.
These things are very old.
People made these many centuries ago.
I move a little further ahead.
There are some small coins in that glass box.
Those coins are made of silver.
I think about the people of that time.
They used these everyday items hundreds of years ago.
Their days were perhaps not very different from my days.
They also bought things in the market with those coins.
They also kept water in these pots.
Time passes, but some things remain the same.
I smile and go toward the next exhibit.
